c1x is a fork of c1 (https://github.com/wurlyfox/c1), a port of Crash Bandicoot to C
by wurlyfox, with contributions from others. Read this whole file: the MIT licence
below does not cover everything in this repository.

What the MIT licence covers
---------------------------

The MIT licence below covers only the changes and additions made in c1x (this fork)
by its contributors: everything in this repository that is not part of the original
c1 port. That includes the launcher, the level editor and level build, the custom
level sources in level_src/, and c1x's changes to the original port's code.

What it does not cover
----------------------

- The original c1 port. Its code, and the reverse engineering behind it, are the work
  of wurlyfox and the port's other contributors. The original repository gives no
  licence, so no licence is granted here for that code, and the MIT licence below
  cannot grant one. Where a file mixes the original port's code with c1x's changes,
  the MIT licence covers only c1x's changes.
- Crash Bandicoot. The game, its name, characters, art, music and other assets
  belong to their owners. c1x is an unofficial fan project that is not affiliated
  with or endorsed by them. No game files are included: the game needs files from
  a copy of Crash Bandicoot you own.
- Third-party code and libraries, such as Dear ImGui and cimgui (in
  src/ext/lib/cimgui) and utest.h (in tests), which keep their own licences, and the
  libraries the game is built with, such as SDL 2 and FluidSynth.

